+++ b/DEVELOPMENT.md
@@ -82,6 +82,36 @@ The flipt binary will check in that location if a `--config` override is not pro
 
 The `USER_CONFIG_DIR` is different based on your architecture, and specified [here](https://pkg.go.dev/os#UserConfigDir).
 
+### OCI snapshot references
+
+For OCI declarative storage, `storage.oci.repository` fixes the scheme, registry,
+repository, and default tag or digest. An empty request reference reads the
+configured default snapshot. Flipt fetches that snapshot during startup and
+polls only that configured reference using `storage.oci.poll_interval`.
+
+A nonempty request reference can be an OCI tag such as `stable` or a complete
+manifest digest such as `sha256:` followed by 64 lowercase hexadecimal digits.
+It is resolved within the configured repository using the configured transport
+and credentials. Repository paths, URLs, alternate schemes, and partial digests
+are rejected. A tag is resolved when each new fetch starts, so a later request
+can observe a moved tag. Concurrent requests for the same tag may share one
+fetch. A digest is immutable and can reuse a verified resident snapshot.
+
+The default snapshot remains resident. Up to three additional reference entries
+are kept in least recently used order. Eviction does not interrupt a `View`
+callback already using a snapshot; each callback receives one complete snapshot.
+The manifest digest identifies the complete registry manifest, including its
+annotations, even when two manifests contain identical layers. A failed fetch
+does not replace a previously published snapshot. Fetches for different
+references can proceed independently.
+
+Closing the OCI snapshot store stops polling and new acquisitions, cancels
+background fetches, and waits for their cleanup. It does not wait for callbacks
+that have already entered `View`; those callbacks retain their snapshots.
+Later `View` calls return `oci.ErrClosed`.
+Fetch closes each acquired registry stream before it returns, including when
+the request is canceled or a descriptor fails validation.
+
 ## Changes
 
 Changing certain types of files such as the proto or ui files require re-building before they will be picked up in new versions of the binary.
